=== b361b84773
Skip automatic setup wizard in JusPrin shell

=== 67577ad993
Add optional printer connection after saving named printers

Keep printer setup receipts separate from connection, expose connect-later actions on Home, and reuse native Bambu and print-host configuration. Preserve saved printers on connection failures and require fresh printer data before confirming Bambu connectivity.

Validation: staged Agent UI snapshot passes 208 tests and production build. Prior native verification passed 313 contract cases and 109 shell integration checks; Home UI passed 52 tests. No upstream production files changed.

=== 4d4f9e466b
Replace printer summary card with conversational setup guidance

=== 2a07ec0fc7
Give printer setup a focused workspace

=== 9f739dccf2
Keep printer connection help available and preserve its provider

Keep the conversation and credential form together, remove redundant device selection and obsolete Add credentials, and distinguish first connection from previously verified communication. Offer host settings and reconnection actions on Home. Report nozzle mismatches without rejecting a live connection; selection interruption and timeout now have separate explanations.

Use GUI_App::switch_printer_agent for explicit connection providers, with a default-empty runtime override that survives slicing-profile changes and is restored on shell teardown. The fork owns provider-selection policy; the existing upstream factory, callback transfer, dropdown refresh and machine-selection behavior remain shared. The upstream footprint is ten additive lines in GUI_App.cpp/.hpp; no upstream lines are removed or relocated. The unchanged default preserves stock profile-driven behavior.

Verification: 214 Agent UI and 55 Home UI tests, both production web builds, 264 native Agent cases, 51 native Home cases, 124 printer integration checks and 25 stock-mode checks passed. Windows Release production DLL and harness built. Light/dark narrow-panel visual review passed. Real network authentication and physical uploads remain outside fake-printer coverage.

Stewardship: merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=8500fcdccaa10b5099ac20d252af3a7c560046f1 against upstream f83bfa17ff878a6689b875353df7200ab2d30053; baseline 4d4f9e466b6a80a780fed6603b0583124f3c53af, working snapshot b250457594e1b3138def53777234bf5ca988ec70, isolated seam 426dec080e5cf61465edeb3e05fc1f88ec85eaa0. Isolated seam merges cleanly (exit 0). Full fork retains nine existing conflicted files with unchanged content-conflict blocks, plus GUI_App.hpp where upstream reworded the switching comment. Keep that comment/declarations and the new runtime field. No history rewrite or Codex configuration change.

On a future upstream replay, preserve its updated provider resolver and fake substitution, applying the explicit choice before provider creation. Its newer resolver uses a const effective ID and different cloud resolution, so port that boundary deliberately instead of blindly retaining assignments. Existing fork conflicts still require preserving both intents in AGENTS.md/CMake/Plater, carrying overlays and relocated rename behavior into upstream's new homes, reconciling translation keys and reviewing the deleted Windows build script. Detailed working evidence remains in the untracked printer-connection-review-fixes-verification.md under repository policy.

